WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.818
Check the domain
Calculate the integral from zero to one of two x divided by one plus x
squared. The denominator is positive, so the integral is well defined.

2
00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:28.273
Choose the substitution
The derivative of the denominator is two x, which appears in the numerator.
This suggests choosing the denominator itself as the new variable.

3
00:00:28.273 --> 00:00:42.182
Transform the differential
Differentiate the relation to obtain dt equal to two x dx. The numerator
together with the differential can therefore be replaced entirely by dt.

4
00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:58.818
Transform the limits
Transform the limits as well. When x is zero, t is one, and when x is one, t
is two. Do not keep the old limits with the new variable.

5
00:00:58.818 --> 00:01:13.182
Integrate
The integral becomes one over t, integrated from one to two. Since t is
positive on this interval, the antiderivative we need is the logarithm.

6
00:01:13.182 --> 00:01:26.182
Calculate and check
Evaluate at the upper limit and subtract the lower-limit value. The logarithm
of one is zero, leaving ln two, positive as expected.
